{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$F, G : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$a : F \\to G$", "MATH_0004": "$a : F \\to G$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjective-flat-locally-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d263b6fb2984478fe3504ede22920d227c6d3e50a0786c7f777a7f7063d730bb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a13d3073b77b088210a034fc9f4b5dff9e1481fdd35f2e05f6a91e0cbe616e8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be sheaves.\nLet <MATH_0003> be representable, flat,\nlocally of finite presentation, and surjective.\nThen <MATH_0004> is surjective as a map of sheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:553cbaadbd8547c2c49dd2512556f380ddc10b12406a9fff5aa97c95e920cc22", "unit_id": "tag:05VM:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$g : T \\to G$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$G$", "MATH_0006": "$T' = F \\times_G T$", "MATH_0007": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$g|_{T'} \\in G(T')$", "MATH_0010": "$F(T')$", "MATH_0011": "$T' \\to F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-sheaves-injective-surjective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75b26c54802ec53789a8592cbb6f55946644b70ef5e143776b92db4524f27c20", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3fec3c24e0ca8a50c1864f30cc21ccd6498f52d4512edff45b5e58e2ede51d15", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme over <MATH_0002> and let <MATH_0003> be a <MATH_0004>-valued point of\n<MATH_0005>. By assumption <MATH_0006> is (representable by) a scheme and\nthe morphism <MATH_0007> is a flat, locally of finite presentation, and\nsurjective. Hence <MATH_0008> is an fppf covering such\nthat <MATH_0009> comes from an element of <MATH_0010>, namely\nthe map <MATH_0011>. This proves the map is surjective as\na map of sheaves, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5be65d132f36a176e65c3b708101d12a7229f2588e957c4511ab78e2c23da93d", "unit_id": "tag:05VM:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ccba419f2f963c6a2bcbd05dcb9c34eaafb6940de0bc8fda6c82e247f26ad02", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is a characterization of those functors for which the\ndiagonal is representable.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:92e1e75ed505b4693c71087ba6cc1aeee653faa9b093b3bb2b921b066dd68ab1", "unit_id": "tag:02WI:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$F \\to F \\times F$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0007": "$a \\in F(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$a : h_U \\to F$", "MATH_0009": "$U, V \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0010": "$a \\in F(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$b \\in F(V)$", "MATH_0012": "$h_U \\times_{a, F, b} h_V$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:315daf242648ad245e13f54e8d113a1d57a21a3158eee199b992bcff3cd314e5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c8a58828dbf45038334c3d80093858de36cb6bc071c3da8c99cbe767030220ec", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0004>.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the diagonal <MATH_0005> is representable,\n<STRUCT_0003> for <MATH_0006> and any <MATH_0007>\nthe map <MATH_0008> is representable,\n<STRUCT_0004> for every pair <MATH_0009>\nand any <MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011> the fibre product\n<MATH_0012> is representable.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d03361d7a931c960f12d82eb40e486bc9be8dfea58072165f50ca2401869342f", "unit_id": "tag:025W:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-fibre-products-fppf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b7e875813bc823b930144ad92ef10071c63bf5ee72ee22d185fe012f8ad2b625", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa18a62292343c9c810485a04a731ec012d5493e872899addd2ffc0e7dd2ccec", "source_text": "This is completely formal, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIt depends only on the fact that the category <MATH_0001>\nhas products of pairs of objects and fibre products, see\nTopologies, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b2f5714543729f30505840630fe82dc3e4571979d4ff824ec2f8ca61b7d4d51b", "unit_id": "tag:025W:proof"}
